# VPN Gateway Responsibilities

VPN Gateway is used to establish secure communication between:
- On-Premises Network
- Azure VNet
- Remote Users
- Other Cloud Networks

It creates encrypted tunnels over the public internet.

---

# 1) Tunnel Creation

VPN Gateway creates:
- IPSec Tunnel
- Secure communication channel

Purpose:
- Protect data while traveling through internet

---

# IPSec Tunnel Flow

On-Premises Network
        |
Encrypted IPSec Tunnel
        |
Azure VPN Gateway
        |
Azure VNet

---

# Tunnel Types

| Type | Purpose |
|------|----------|
| Site-to-Site (S2S) | Office to Azure |
| Point-to-Site (P2S) | Individual user to Azure |
| VNet-to-VNet | Azure VNet communication |

---

# 2) Encryption

VPN Gateway encrypts data before sending.

Purpose:
- Prevent attackers from reading data

Uses:
- IPSec
- AES Encryption

---

# Encryption Flow

Original Data
      |
Encryption
      |
Cipher Text
      |
Internet
      |
Azure VPN Gateway

Even if intercepted:
- Data cannot be understood.

---

# 3) Decryption

At destination:
- VPN Gateway decrypts encrypted packets.

Flow:

Encrypted Packet
       |
VPN Gateway
       |
Decryption
       |
Original Data

---

# 4) Authentication

VPN Gateway verifies:
- User
- Device
- Network

before allowing connection.

---

# Authentication Methods

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|----------|
| Pre-Shared Key (PSK) | Shared secret key |
| Certificates | Secure authentication |
| Azure AD | User authentication |

---

# Authentication Flow

Client
   |
Identity Verification
   |
VPN Gateway
   |
Connection Allowed

---

# 5) Routing

VPN Gateway routes traffic between:
- Azure VNet
- On-Premises Network

---

# Example

Azure VNet:
10.0.0.0/16

On-Prem:
192.168.1.0/24

VPN Gateway routes traffic between both networks.

